---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Hero from '../components/Hero.astro';
import UVScale from '../components/UVScale.astro';
import EvidenceNote from '../components/EvidenceNote.astro';
import StoreButton from '../components/StoreButton.astro';
import { SITE, absoluteUrl, organizationSchema } from '../config';

const jsonLd = [
  {
    '@context': 'https://schema.org',
    '@type': 'SoftwareApplication',
    name: SITE.name,
    applicationCategory: 'HealthApplication',
    operatingSystem: 'iOS',
    url: absoluteUrl('/'),
    offers: {
      '@type': 'Offer',
      price: '0',
      priceCurrency: 'USD',
    },
    downloadUrl: SITE.appStoreUrl,
    publisher: organizationSchema(),
  },
  organizationSchema(),
];
---

<BaseLayout
  locale="en"
  path="/"
  title="Bronzla · Know your safe time in the sun"
  description="Bronzla works out how long you can safely stay in the sun today, from the current UV index, your Fitzpatrick skin type and your SPF. Free on the App Store, no ads, no subscription, no in-app purchases."
  jsonLd={jsonLd}
>
  <Hero locale="en" />

  {/* Open section. The heading hangs in its own column and the argument runs beside it. */}
  <section class="container statement">
    <div class="statement-head">
      <p class="eyebrow">The method</p>
      <h2>A number, not a guess</h2>
    </div>
    <div class="statement-body">
      <p>
        "Stay out of the midday sun" is advice nobody can actually follow. Bronzla replaces it
        with a number: the minutes you have today, worked out from the UV index where you are,
        your Fitzpatrick skin type and the SPF you're wearing. It caps every recommendation at 60
        per cent of the calculated burn time and never suggests more than three hours, whatever
        the arithmetic says.
      </p>
      <p>
        A seven-question quiz determines your Fitzpatrick type without asking you to eyeball a
        chart. The questions are written for the olive and wheat tones common along the
        Mediterranean and Aegean coasts, on their own terms rather than against northern European
        reference points.
      </p>
      <a class="text-link" href="/science/">Read the full method and citation list</a>
    </div>
  </section>

  {/* Dense panel, second elevation. Deliberately tight after the open section above it. */}
  <section class="container timer-section">
    <div class="panel timer-panel">
      <div class="timer-head">
        <p class="eyebrow">Timer</p>
        <h2>Reminders that work with the screen off</h2>
        <p class="timer-intro">
          Flip and sunscreen reminders that work with the phone in your bag and the screen off.
          The remaining time stays live on your lock screen.
        </p>
      </div>
      <ul class="timer-list">
        <li>
          <h3>Flip reminder</h3>
          <p>A nudge to turn, so both sides get an even dose through the session.</p>
        </li>
        <li>
          <h3>Sunscreen reminder</h3>
          <p>A prompt to reapply every two hours, sooner after swimming or towelling.</p>
        </li>
        <li>
          <h3>Live on the lock screen</h3>
          <p>The countdown keeps running and stays visible without unlocking the phone.</p>
        </li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="container uv-section ruled">
    <div class="uv-head">
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow eyebrow-signal">UV forecast</p>
        <h2>See a burn coming</h2>
      </div>
      <p class="uv-lede">
        Hourly and ten day UV forecasts, with the riskiest hours of the day called out plainly, so
        you can see a burn coming before you leave the house. Every reading maps to the same five
        WHO bands the app uses everywhere else, coloured to rise in luminance with severity so the
        scale still reads correctly for colour vision deficiency.
      </p>
    </div>
    <UVScale locale="en" />
  </section>

  <section class="container evidence-section ruled">
    <div class="evidence-head">
      <p class="eyebrow">Evidence</p>
      <h2>Where the numbers come from</h2>
    </div>
    <EvidenceNote locale="en" />
    <a class="text-link" href="/science/">See the full method, worked examples and sources</a>
  </section>

  {/* The statement shape again, deliberately: two uses of one layout across a page is a
      system, whereas six uses of one layout is a template. */}
  <section class="container privacy-section">
    <div class="statement-head">
      <p class="eyebrow">Privacy</p>
      <h2>No account, because there is nowhere to send your data</h2>
    </div>
    <div class="privacy-body">
      <p>
        There is no server behind Bronzla. Your skin type, your session history and your tan
        tracker photos stay in local storage on your phone. Location is used only to ask Apple
        WeatherKit for the UV index where you are; it is never linked to an identity, and you can
        skip it entirely and pick a city instead. No analytics SDK, no advertising, no third party
        of any kind.
      </p>
      <a class="text-link" href="/privacy/">Read the full privacy page</a>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="container closing-section">
    <div class="panel closing-cta">
      <h2>Free. No ads, no subscription, no in-app purchases.</h2>
      <StoreButton locale="en" size="large" />
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  /*
   * Section density is composed, not repeated: open statement, dense panel, tight strip,
   * tight evidence, open statement, closing panel. A single padding value on every section
   * is the thing that makes a page read as generated.
   */
  .statement {
    padding-block: 0 var(--space-open);
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 0.85fr) minmax(0, 1.15fr);
    gap: clamp(2rem, 5vw, 5rem);
    align-items: start;
  }

  .statement-head {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 1rem;
  }

  .statement-head h2 {
    max-width: 12ch;
  }

  .statement-body {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    align-items: flex-start;
    gap: 1.25rem;
    max-width: 52ch;
  }

  .statement-body p {
    color: var(--ink-muted);
  }

  .statement-body p:first-child {
    font-size: var(--text-lede);
    line-height: 1.5;
    color: var(--ink);
    max-width: none;
  }

  .timer-section {
    padding-block: 0 var(--space-section);
  }

  .timer-panel {
    padding: clamp(1.75rem, 4vw, 3rem);
  }

  .timer-head {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 0.85rem;
    max-width: 46rem;
  }

  .timer-head h2 {
    font-size: var(--text-h3);
    max-width: 22ch;
  }

  .timer-intro {
    color: var(--ink-muted);
    max-width: 60ch;
  }

  /*
   * Plain type divided by hairlines, never three icon-topped cards: DESIGN.md bans the
   * identical card grid, and the panel around them already supplies the container.
   */
  .timer-list {
    list-style: none;
    margin: clamp(1.75rem, 3vw, 2.5rem) 0 0;
    padding: 0;
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(3, minmax(0, 1fr));
    border-top: 1px solid var(--hairline);
  }

  .timer-list li {
    padding: 1.5rem 1.5rem 0 0;
  }

  .timer-list li + li {
    padding-left: 1.5rem;
    border-left: 1px solid var(--hairline);
  }

  .timer-list h3 {
    font-size: var(--text-body);
    font-weight: var(--weight-strong);
  }

  .timer-list p {
    color: var(--ink-muted);
    font-size: var(--text-small);
    margin-top: 0.5rem;
  }

  .uv-section {
    padding-block: var(--space-section);
  }

  .uv-head {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 0.8fr) minmax(0, 1.2fr);
    gap: clamp(1.5rem, 4vw, 4rem);
    align-items: end;
    margin-bottom: clamp(1.5rem, 3vw, 2.25rem);
  }

  .uv-head h2 {
    font-size: var(--text-h2);
    max-width: 10ch;
    margin-top: 0.85rem;
  }

  .uv-lede {
    color: var(--ink-muted);
    max-width: 58ch;
  }

  /* The tightest block on the page, immediately after the widest. */
  .evidence-section {
    padding-block: var(--space-tight);
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    align-items: flex-start;
    gap: 1.25rem;
  }

  /*
   * Still an h2 for the document outline, set at h3 size: this block is a footnote to the
   * page, and the outline should not be bent to suit the type scale.
   */
  .evidence-head {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 0.75rem;
  }

  .evidence-head h2 {
    font-size: var(--text-h3);
  }

  .evidence-section :global(.evidence-note) {
    align-self: stretch;
  }

  .privacy-section {
    padding-block: var(--space-section) var(--space-open);
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 0.85fr) minmax(0, 1.15fr);
    gap: clamp(2rem, 5vw, 5rem);
    align-items: start;
  }

  .privacy-section h2 {
    max-width: 14ch;
  }

  /*
   * Set in two columns rather than one long measure: the same shape as the statement
   * section would read as a repeat, and a short passage sets well in columns.
   */
  .privacy-body {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    align-items: flex-start;
    gap: 1.25rem;
    max-width: 52ch;
  }

  .privacy-body p {
    font-size: var(--text-lede);
    line-height: 1.5;
    color: var(--ink-muted);
    max-width: none;
  }

  .closing-section {
    padding-block: 0 var(--space-section);
  }

  .closing-cta {
    padding: clamp(2.5rem, 6vw, 4.5rem) clamp(1.75rem, 4vw, 3rem);
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: space-between;
    gap: 2rem;
  }

  .closing-cta h2 {
    max-width: 16ch;
  }

  @media (max-width: 60rem) {
    .statement,
    .privacy-section,
    .uv-head {
      grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr);
    }

    .uv-head {
      align-items: start;
    }
  }

  @media (max-width: 48rem) {
    .timer-list {
      grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr);
    }

    .timer-list li {
      padding-right: 0;
    }

    .timer-list li + li {
      padding-left: 0;
      border-left: none;
      border-top: 1px solid var(--hairline);
    }
  }
</style>
